# Wireshark profile for the ESP32-C6 Bluetooth LE interface.
#
# One profile per radio: a filter button belongs to the profile, not to the
# interface, so a shared profile shows buttons that cannot match. This one
# switches itself in on the BLE interface -- see profile_settings.
#
# The default Source and Destination columns are useless here: every frame is
# "controller -> host", because this is an HCI capture and the transport is
# always the same pair. The advertiser's address is the thing worth seeing, so
# it takes their place.
#
# No channel column: the controller rotates the three advertising channels
# itself and does not report which one a report came from.
#
# Address kind and Maker tell the devices in a capture apart. Wireshark's
# filter bar cannot hold a list that fills itself from the capture, so these
# are that list: sort by a column to group its devices, right-click a cell
# and Apply as Filter to see one device, one maker or one kind of address.
# Address kind is where a device the board follows by its key shows up, as an
# identity address instead of the private one it sent.

gui.column.format:
	"No.", "%m",
	"Time", "%t",
	"RSSI", "%Cus:bthci_evt.rssi:0:R",
	"Advertiser", "%Cus:bthci_evt.bd_addr:0:R",
	"Address kind", "%Cus:bthci_evt.le_peer_address_type:0:R",
	"Maker", "%Cus:btcommon.eir_ad.entry.company_id:0:R",
	"Name", "%Cus:btcommon.eir_ad.entry.device_name:0:R",
	"Iface", "%Cus:frame.interface_name:0:R",
	"Protocol", "%p",
	"Len", "%L",
	"Info", "%i"
